findings.recommended_change:
Invert the trigger. If rung 2 gives geometry but no task gain at N ≥ 3 with guards held, record 'construction is not a task-metric limiter'. Keep the bounded head only if it improves motion quality, and stop algorithm work.

Further algorithm work (other heads, FPO++, off-policy) needs all of the following:
- (a) a task block BETTER at the seed-inflated R (T 1.13, F 3.19, F_mt 4.12 z), pooled over ≥ 3 seeds and surviving to lineage length;
- (b) the predicted mechanism visible in rung-0 telemetry: late behavioural KL share up from 0.11-0.16, LR off the floor, executed change per update ≥ 2×;
- (c) the gain not reproduced by an action_rate-only control;
- (d) a residual failure, after canonical training, that optimizer telemetry separates. Today no task row of §4.8 has such a separator.

For a family swap, additionally show that wall-clock or sample count is the binding constraint.

Merge rung 4 into rung 1. Adopt a larger env count once, as an infrastructure change with one budgeted re-baseline, not as a hyper-parameter screen.

Kill env scaling if any of these hold:
- wall time per iteration at 1024 envs > 1.5× the 256-env 1.318 s;
- VRAM > 10 GB, which would leave no room for 3-4 GB concurrent evals;
- NaN or dead_plant within 200 iterations.

For every surviving rung, pre-register before launch:
- the predicted sign on each task block;
- the mechanism read, with its iteration and threshold;
- the kill read.

Record misses in the ledger as prediction failures.
